request.description:
### Update Tenant Inventory

This endpoint allows the client to update the inventory for a specific tenant.

#### Request Body

- `tenantId` (number) - The ID of the tenant.

- `type` (string) - The type of inventory update, e.g., "move-out".

- `items` (array) - An array of objects containing the details of the items being updated, including `name` (string), `quantity` (number), and `condition` (string).

- `notes` (string) - Additional notes related to the inventory update.


#### Response

The response will be in JSON format with the following schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "success": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "inventory": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "tenantId": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "items": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "quantity": {
                "type": "number"
              },
              "condition": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "checkedBy": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "notes": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "createdAt": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "updatedAt": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

### POST /api/tenant-inventory

This endpoint is used to submit the inventory details for a specific tenant.

#### Request Body

- tenantId (number): The ID of the tenant.

- type (string): The type of inventory (e.g., move-in, move-out).

- items (array): An array of objects containing the details of each item in the inventory, including name, condition, and quantity.

- notes (string): Additional notes related to the inventory submission.


#### Response

The response will be in the form of a JSON schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "success": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "inventory": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "tenantId": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "type": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "items": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "condition": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "quantity": {
                "type": "number"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "checkedBy": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "notes": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "updatedAt": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "createdAt": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

